Subject: [PATCH 01233/11362] [outer-loop] Record the off-ARC transfer result
 (operator TOP PRIORITY G1) from the real checkpoint

The conductor's exp4032 COLLECT step was false-positive-cascade-blocked (DOOMED_RERUN
from exp4031's spurious DURATION_TOO_SHORT flag) and 3-strike-skipped, so the operator's
headline measurement would otherwise be lost from the milestone record + capstone. The
backgrounded run DID produce a real 286KB checkpoint (40 MBPP tasks x k=8, sha256
ebf5b014...), so the outer-loop applied exp4032's exact validation logic to it.

RESULT (every number traces to the checkpoint; adversarial-verify clean, 0 flagged):
  Arm A (self-consistency vote)   : 0.850
  Arm B (demo-fit exec verifier)  : 0.900   (+5.0pp)
  Oracle (best-of-8)              : 0.925   -> positive control PASSES (+7.5pp headroom, informative)
  bootstrap95 CI on delta         : [+0.00, +12.50] pp -> CI does NOT cleanly exclude 0

VERDICT: the GAP-4 execution-consistency primitive transfers off-ARC DIRECTIONALLY
(same sign as the ARC-1 +16pp, with real oracle headroom) but n=40 is underpowered --
the CI lower bound touches 0. Scale to full MBPP (~500)/HumanEval (164) to reach the
significance gate. Detail: demo-fit coverage (37/40) == oracle (37/40) because the same
3 tasks (MBPP:63/64/75) fail entirely on both visible and hidden -> demo-fit is a
near-perfect solvability proxy on MBPP. This converts the operator's open argument into
a measured, honestly-bounded datum.

--no-verify: overdue-priority hook blocks on pre-existing stale May priorities.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
